  "narrative": {
    "intro": "W S Darley and recorded $935M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Obligations fell 37.0% year over year. Award activity includes 1,758 actions and an average award size of $532K. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligated $929M. Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers is the largest market at $490M, followed by All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing at $408M. Recent fiscal-year history shows growth up to $1.5B in FY25 and a partial-year total of $935M in FY26. This profile shows a heavy reliance on one agency and a narrow set of markets for federal business, with current-year totals marked as fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How concentrated are W S Darley and's federal obligations?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense accounts for $929M of obligations in FY2026 to date. The next-largest buyer is the General Services Administration at $4M, so buying is highly concentrated. Obligations by fiscal year rose from $431M in FY21 to $1.5B in FY25 before returning to $935M in FY26."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets drive W S Darley and's federal revenue?",
        "body": "Service Establishment Equipment and Supplies Merchant Wholesalers drives $490M in FY2026 to date. All Other Miscellaneous Manufacturing contributes $408M, with smaller contributions from Photographic and Photocopying Equipment Manufacturing at $13.4M and Surgical Appliance and Supplies Manufacturing at $10.7M."
      }
    ]
